er the main parsing functions. Writing the validation function...\n\nI'm checking whether `evalSymbolic` with `current=0` properly handles the `X` flag — it should validate syntax without erroring, since `X` is conditionally applied based on the file's actual mode at runtime, not during validation. &0111 != 0`. With 0, this is false, so X is a no-op. But X should also trigger on directories. Looking at the GNU chmod behavior: `X` sets execute only if the file is a directory OR if any execute bit is already set. The current implementation in `buildMask` only checks `current&0111 != 0`, which misses the directory check. But that's a separate bug in mode.go (R1.2 scope), not related to R4 validation.\n\nFor validation purposes, `evalSymbolic(mode, 0, 0)` with umask=0 correctly identifies syntax errors. Any syntactically valid mode will parse without error regardless of the current/umask values. ✓\n\nThe `strconv.ParseUint` error message would include details like \"value out of range\", but we don't actually use that — `main()` prints our own formatted message instead, so only the nil/non-nil status matters. ✓\n\nNow I'm ready to implement the changes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16095,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16095},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1fb9aa0-d443-4fb0-adfd-577584f3890c","uuid":"afa95abd-cf80-4a28-be08-5113f61546a3"}
